IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (NSW) -- the shared nouns, and s 3B (which claims the Act's provisions apply to).
--
-- SEAT: the injured person (or, in Part 1B and Part 1C, the person abused as a child) bringing a claim for damages.
-- Every exported question is one that person would ask. Courts, insurers and organisations get no seat: what the Act
-- lets them do is encoded as what it means for the claimant.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "unless" or "only", a flat "do not apply"), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to the court are asked as the
-- court's finding, with "the court has not decided" answering NOTHING.
--
-- Dates use only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL), not the daydate library.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025, corpus version dated 16 June 2022; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Liability Act 2002 -- shared nouns and s 3B`

§§ `Arithmetic and dates`

GIVEN `the first number` IS A NUMBER, `the second number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `the first number` `and` `the second number` MEANS
    IF `the first number` AT MOST `the second number` THEN `the first number` ELSE `the second number`

-- Whole numbers: the s 16 Table speaks only of whole percentages.
GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a whole number` `the number` IF TRUNC `the number` 0 EQUALS `the number`

-- s 16(4), s 17(5): "rounded to the nearest $500 (with the amounts of $250 and $750 being rounded up)". For a
-- non-negative amount that is: add $250 and drop to the $500 at or below.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest 500 dollars` `the amount` MEANS
    (TRUNC ((`the amount` PLUS 250) DIVIDED BY 500) 0) TIMES 500

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the count` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `the count` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS `the count`)

§§ `Shared answers`

-- A judgment the Act leaves to the court ("if the court is satisfied", "just and reasonable", "reasonable precautions"),
-- asked as the court's finding.
DECLARE `The court's finding` IS ONE OF
    `the court has found that it is so`
    `the court has found that it is not so`
    `the court has not decided`

-- An amount the Act fixes or caps, or why it gives none.
DECLARE `Amount under the section` IS ONE OF
    `the amount is` HAS `the figure` IS A NUMBER
    `this section does not apply to my claim`
    `the Act does not settle the amount`

§§ `The kinds of claim s 3B sorts`

-- s 3B(1) lists civil liability to which the Act, or parts of it, do not apply. The claimant states which kind of claim
-- theirs is. "The defendant's own" intentional act matters: s 3B(1)(a) speaks of "civil liability of a person in respect
-- of an intentional act that is done by the person". Whether it reaches an organisation's vicarious liability for
-- someone else's act is not said (fork F1).
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here`
    `an intentional act the defendant did meaning to injure or kill`
    `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant`
    `vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct`
    `a dust disease claim of the kind brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal`
    `injury or death from smoking or other use of tobacco products`
    `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
    `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 or the Motor Accidents Act 1988`
    `work injury damages against an employer under Division 3 of Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987`
    `statutory compensation or a statutory benefit`

-- The provisions s 3B keeps or excludes, grouped as s 3B groups them.
DECLARE `Part of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `Part 1A Divisions 1 to 4 and 8: negligence, causation, obvious and inherent risks, contributory negligence`
    `Part 1A Divisions 5 to 7: recreational activities, professional negligence, non-delegable duties`
    `Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse`
    `Part 1C: setting aside child abuse settlements`
    `section 15: gratuitous attendant care`
    `section 15A: gratuitous attendant care in dust disease claims`
    `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
    `section 15C: lost employer superannuation contributions`
    `section 16: damages for non-economic loss`
    `section 17A: earlier awards for non-economic loss`
    `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services`
    `the rest of Part 2: earnings cap, discount rate, other interest rules, third party contributions, no exemplary damages`
    `Part 2 Division 7: structured settlements`
    `Part 3: mental harm`
    `section 49: intoxication and the duty and standard of care`
    `the rest of Part 6: no recovery when intoxicated`
    `Part 7: self-defence and recovery by criminals`
    `Part 8: good samaritans`
    `another Part of the Act`

§§ `s 3B -- civil liability excluded from the Act`

-- s 3B(2): "The following provisions apply to motor accidents": Part 1A Divs 1-4 and 8; s 15B and s 15C (except for a
-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 accident); s 17A; s 18(1) as to s 18(1)(c); Part 2 Div 7; Part 3; s 49; Part 7;
-- Part 8.
GIVEN `the part` IS A `Part of the Act`, `under the 2017 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3B(2) keeps` `the part` `for a motor accident` `under the 2017 Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `Part 1A Divisions 1 to 4 and 8: negligence, causation, obvious and inherent risks, contributory negligence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants` THEN NOT `under the 2017 Act`
    WHEN `section 15C: lost employer superannuation contributions` THEN NOT `under the 2017 Act`
    WHEN `section 17A: earlier awards for non-economic loss` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 2 Division 7: structured settlements` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 3: mental harm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 49: intoxication and the duty and standard of care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 7: self-defence and recovery by criminals` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 8: good samaritans` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3B(1) for a defendant's own act. (a) intentional act with intent to injure or kill, or sexual assault or other sexual
-- misconduct: the whole Act except Part 1B, s 15B, s 18(1) as to s 18(1)(c), Part 2A, and Part 7 (Part 7 only for an act
-- done with intent to injure or kill). (b) dust diseases: the whole Act except ss 15A, 15B, 18(1) as to s 18(1)(c).
-- (c) tobacco: the whole Act except s 15B and s 18(1) as to s 18(1)(c). (d), (e), (e1) motor accidents: s 3B(2).
-- (f) work injury damages: the whole Act other than Part 1B. (g), (h) statutory compensation and benefits: the whole Act.
GIVEN `the part` IS A `Part of the Act`, `the claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3B leaves` `the part` `applying to a claim of kind` `the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an intentional act the defendant did meaning to injure or kill` THEN
              `the part` EQUALS `Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `Part 7: self-defence and recovery by criminals`
    WHEN `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant` THEN
              `the part` EQUALS `Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services`
    WHEN `a dust disease claim of the kind brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` THEN
              `the part` EQUALS `section 15A: gratuitous attendant care in dust disease claims`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services`
    WHEN `injury or death from smoking or other use of tobacco products` THEN
              `the part` EQUALS `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
           OR `the part` EQUALS `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services`
    WHEN `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017` THEN `s 3B(2) keeps` `the part` `for a motor accident` TRUE
    WHEN `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 or the Motor Accidents Act 1988` THEN `s 3B(2) keeps` `the part` `for a motor accident` FALSE
    WHEN `work injury damages against an employer under Division 3 of Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987` THEN
           `the part` EQUALS `Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3B(1) "The provisions of this Act do not apply to or in respect of civil liability ... as follows": a flat negative,
-- so an excluded part answers JUST FALSE. For vicarious liability for someone else's intentional or sexual act, the
-- answer is the general one where (a) would make no difference, and NOTHING where it would (fork F1).
@export Does this part of the Civil Liability Act apply to my claim, as far as section 3B goes (s 3B)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What your claim is. One of: "negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here"; "an intentional act the defendant did meaning to injure or kill"; "sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant"; "vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct" (for example a claim against an employer for an employee's abuse); "a dust disease claim of the kind brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal"; "injury or death from smoking or other use of tobacco products"; "a motor accident claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017"; "a motor accident claim under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 or the Motor Accidents Act 1988"; "work injury damages against an employer under Division 3 of Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987" (not a child abuse claim, which that Division does not cover); "statutory compensation or a statutory benefit" (workers compensation, dust diseases compensation, anti-discrimination compensation, a sporting injuries benefit, or victims support for economic loss)
      `the part I am asking about` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc The part of the Act you are asking about, for example "section 16: damages for non-economic loss" or "Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` MEANS
    IF `my kind of claim` EQUALS `vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct`
    THEN IF     (`s 3B leaves` `the part I am asking about` `applying to a claim of kind` `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here`)
            AND (`s 3B leaves` `the part I am asking about` `applying to a claim of kind` `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: whether s 3B(1)(a) reaches liability for another person's act; fork F1)
    ELSE IF `s 3B leaves` `the part I am asking about` `applying to a claim of kind` `my kind of claim`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Used by the other modules: TRUE / FALSE / open, from s 3B, for one part.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Kind of claim`, `the part` IS A `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3B answer for` `the claim` `and` `the part` MEANS `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `the claim` `the part`
